     "n": 20,
     "section": "Database",
     "page": 3,
     "q": "What do you understand by Functional dependency?",
     "a": "A relation is said to be in functional dependency when one attribute uniquely defines another\nattribute.\nFor Example, R is a Relation, X and Y are two attributes. T1 and T2 are two tuples. Then,\nT1[X]=T2[X] and T1[Y]=T2[Y]\nMeans, the value of component X uniquely define the value of component Y.\nAlso, X->Y means Y is functionally dependent on X."
