     "q": "Why is a URL encoded in HTML?",
     "a": "An URL is encoded to convert non-ASCII characters into a format that can be used over the Internet because\na URL is sent over the Internet by using the ASCII character-set only. If a URL contains characters outside\nthe ASCII set, the URL has to be converted. The non-ASCII characters are replaced with a “%” followed by\nhexadecimal digits."
