     "a": "White spaces are a blank sequence of space characters, which is treated as a single space character in HTML.\nBecause the browser collapses multiple spaces into a single space, you can indent lines of text without\nworrying about multiple spaces. This enables you to organize the HTML code into a much more readable\nformat."
