     "n": 31,
     "section": "Node.js",
     "page": 7,
     "q": "Why is a buffer class used in Node.js?",
     "a": "A buffer class is primarily used as a way to store data in Node.js. This can be considered as a similar\nimplementation of arrays or lists. Here, the class refers to a raw memory location that is not present in the\nV8 heap structure.\nThe buffer class is global, thereby extending its usage across all the modules of an application."
