     "n": 34,
     "section": "Node.js",
     "page": 8,
     "q": "What are streams in Node.js?",
     "a": "Streams are a set of data entities in Node.js. These can be considered similar to the working of strings and\narray objects. Streams are used for continuous read/write operations across a channel. But, if the channel\nis unavailable, all the data cannot be pushed to the memory at once. Hence, using streams will make it easy\nto process a large set of data in a continuous manner.\ncategory of questions."
