     "page": 1,
     "q": "Is PHP a case sensitive language?",
     "a": "PHP is partially case sensitive. The variable names are case-sensitive but function names are not. If you\ndefine the function name in lowercase and call them in uppercase, it will still work. User-defined functions\nare not case sensitive but the rest of the language is case-sensitive."
